<!--Post: 3149--><!--Time: 1104517118-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3149"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Racefan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Racefan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 10:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->has anyone seen or heard anything on the letters that have been sent recently that would prove they have been written lately? i mean how do know that these are not just old letters that where written by him back when he was doing the murders but just never sent them? my point is what do they have to prove he is still alive? <BR>what if someone just came across his &#34;trophies&#34; in an old trunk or box and wants to get rid of them so the rest of the family wouldn&#39;t find out the truth about their &#34;uncle,dad,brother,and so on&#34;  <BR>really wouldn&#39;t make sense that they would not just contact the police first but if they fear public attention or hate towards them they may just try to get rid of it. <BR>i just think BTK could be dead and could have written all these clues years ago. show us proof that he has dated something in a letter that is in 2004.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3149-->
<!--Post: 3163--><!--Time: 1104535528-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3163"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bargle<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bargle<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 3:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s subjective, but BTK has included a chapter list in 2 of his communications from this year. If we are correct in thinking the lists are inspired by the ones at the Crime Library site, then that would put them as having been written after the creation of that site which I think was in the late 90s.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3163-->
<!--Post: 3167--><!--Time: 1104537668-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3167"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 4:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;BTK is monitoring the papers and the electronic media...&#34; Wichita Police Chief Norman Williams to Wichita Eagle Reporter Tim Potter 12-30-04. <BR>So the key word is is. He is monitoring. They must have written evidence that they have conclusively linked to the BTK suspect that refers to current events. BTK is obviously commenting on newspaper articles and the electronic media must also include the internet as well as televison or Williams would have said more simply that BTK is reading the papers and watching news reports. Monitoring the electronic media implies more than reading papers and watching television news coverage.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3167-->
<!--Post: 3761--><!--Time: 1105195452-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3761"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 08, 2005 - 6:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Racefan <BR> <BR>I think if a familymeber found out that their dead relative was BTK and wanted to cover it up, keep it a secret I think they would burn the findings or digg a deep hole and get rid of it NOT start som HUGE media circus. <BR> <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3761-->
<!--Post: 3994--><!--Time: 1105506926-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3994"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nadeltanz<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nadeltanz<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 9:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s always good to keep an open mind. There is <BR>some truth in what Racefan is saying.  Someone other than B. could be dropping off these letters. It <BR>doesn&#39;t hurt to keep more than one theory in mind. <BR>Nadeltanz<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3994-->
